1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
For years, students have had to adapt to
the lesson.

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,020
Memorize a formula.

3
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:05,540
Follow the steps.

4
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:07,780
Move on — even when it never clicks.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,500
What if the lesson could adapt instead?

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,470
Why Math begins teaching, listens to the
student,

7
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:16,680
and changes the next explanation.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,980
Here are two simulated students.

9
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:21,280
Both fourteen.

10
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:23,880
Both starting from the same math idea.

11
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:26,290
Student A needs the words explained.

12
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:29,090
Student B has a different
misunderstanding.

13
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:32,730
One AI teacher responds to what each
student actually says.

14
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:34,920
It does not see their hidden test
profiles.

15
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,470
The same teacher works in Korean, too.

16
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:41,390
Questions are not failures.

17
00:00:41,390 --> 00:00:45,570
When a learner is unsure, the lesson
explains rather than rushing ahead.

18
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,890
Some ideas are easier to see.

19
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:50,370
Add an apple.

20
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:52,250
Take it away. Now the basket is empty.

21
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:53,940
That quantity has a name: zero.

22
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,450
Your Living Textbook grows automatically,

23
00:00:57,450 --> 00:00:59,190
saving the explanations, questions,

24
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:01,790
and what still needs checking —

25
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:03,590
not inventing mastery scores.

26
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,220
Same mathematics.

27
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:08,790
Different minds. A path that adapts to
you.

28
00:01:08,790 --> 00:01:10,500
Explore Why Math on GitHub.
